<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    ==============================================================================================
    PowerFramework.Shared.Localization.Tests
    ==============================================================================================
    Unit test project for PowerFramework.Shared.Localization, the .NET port of the legacy
    PowerBuilder localization surface. The behavioural specification is the read-only legacy tree:

      ws_objects/pfw.ui.pbl.src/n_cst_i18n.sru                    provider contract, a single event
                                                                  member ontranslate(source,
                                                                  category, ref text) at L9
      ws_objects/pfw.ui.pbl.src/i18n.srf                          the three overload facade, with
                                                                  the silent passthrough fallback
                                                                  when no provider is installed
      ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/ne_cst_i18n.sru       CAT_MSGBOX and CAT_DWSVC as
                                                                  offsets from I18N_CAT_CUSTOM
      ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/n_cst_i18n_en.sru     English provider, including the
                                                                  two preserved mistranslations
      ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/n_cst_i18n_chs.sru    Simplified Chinese, the base
                                                                  locale, a genuine no operation
      ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/n_cst_i18n_cht.sru    Traditional Chinese table lookup
      pfw.i18n.xml                                                the translation resource table

    HAND AUTHORED, DELIBERATELY. No template can produce this project: `dotnet new xunit3` does not
    exist in SDK 10.0.302, and `dotnet new xunit` scaffolds the xunit v2 line with older test SDK
    and coverage packages. Do not regenerate this file from a template and patch it.

    INHERITED, NEVER RESTATED. TargetFramework (net10.0), LangVersion, Nullable, ImplicitUsings,
    TreatWarningsAsErrors and ManagePackageVersionsCentrally all arrive by MSBuild directory walkup
    from the repository root Directory.Build.props, which declares no Import element and therefore
    terminates the walkup. Restating any of them here would be duplication; weakening any of them
    would break a repository wide quality gate. That is why this file contains no NoWarn property
    and no TargetFramework, and why every package reference below is versionless.

    No credential material of any kind appears in this file, and none may ever be added to it. The
    project declares no configuration values at all, which is what keeps that guarantee trivial.
    ==============================================================================================
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>

    <!--
      MANDATORY for xunit.v3, and the single property that distinguishes a v3 test project from a
      v2 one. The v3 runner supplies its own application entry point, so the test assembly must be
      an executable. Built as a library it never starts, and `dotnet test` discovers zero tests.
    -->
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>

    <!-- A test assembly is never published to a package feed. -->
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>

    <!-- Declares the project to `dotnet test` and the VSTest platform as a test project. -->
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>

    <!--
      AssemblyName and RootNamespace are deliberately left unset: the SDK already derives both as
      PowerFramework.Shared.Localization.Tests from this file's name, which is exactly the intended
      value, and the nine test source files in this folder declare that namespace.
    -->

  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Test stack. Every reference is deliberately VERSIONLESS. Central package management is enabled
    repository wide, so the single source of truth for versions is the repository root
    Directory.Packages.props, which pins xunit.v3 3.2.2, xunit.runner.visualstudio 3.1.5,
    Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 18.8.1 and coverlet.collector 10.0.1. Adding a Version attribute here
    would raise an NU1008 class error and defeat the mechanism that forces the repository's
    mandatory security pins onto every project from one place.

    coverlet.collector is what makes `dotnet test` with the XPlat Code Coverage collector emit
    coverage.cobertura.xml, the artifact the line coverage gate is measured from. See docs/BUILD.md
    for the exact command; it cannot be spelled here because an MSBuild comment may not contain two
    consecutive hyphens.

    The list is exhaustive by design, and matches the sibling shared library test projects:
      * No Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing. A shared library exposes no HTTP surface, so there is
        no in process host to spin up.
      * No XML or XPath package. The resource reader under test uses System.Xml.Linq together with
        System.Xml.XPath, both of which ship inside the Microsoft.NETCore.App shared framework. A
        package reference here would be the first thread of coupling to a deferred capability that
        this phase must not implement even partially.
      * No mocking or fluent assertion library. The test doubles in this folder are hand written
        classes (FakeI18nProviders.cs) and assertions use xunit's own Assert.
      * No logging, parser or pinyin package. Nothing in this project needs one.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <PackageReference Include="coverlet.collector" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Exactly one project reference: the system under test, and nothing else.

    PowerFramework.Shared.Kernel arrives transitively through it, which is how these tests reach
    RetCode.OK, RetCode.E_INVALID_OBJECT, Enums.I18N_SRC_PFW, Enums.I18N_SRC_CUSTOM, the
    Enums.I18N_CAT_* set and Formatting.Sprintf. A direct reference to Kernel would be redundant
    and would misstate this project's dependency shape, so it is deliberately absent, as is any
    reference to a sibling shared library. One test assembly covers one shared library, so
    coverage is never merged across libraries and the per project gate cannot be masked.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../PowerFramework.Shared.Localization/PowerFramework.Shared.Localization.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Translation resource fixture.

    The legacy providers load the resource table by BARE RELATIVE FILENAME from the process working
    directory: `_doc.LoadFile("pfw.i18n.xml")` at n_cst_i18n_en.sru:159 and at
    n_cst_i18n_cht.sru:63. The xunit.v3 test host runs with the build output directory as its
    working directory, so linking the repository root resource to that same bare filename
    reproduces the legacy lookup exactly and lets the reader tests assert on the relative filename
    with zero path arithmetic in test code.

    Why a Content link to the single real file, and never a checked in duplicate:

      * The repository root pfw.i18n.xml is part of the read-only legacy tree and is the
        behavioural oracle for parity. MSBuild only ever COPIES it into the output directory.
        Nothing in this project writes to, moves, renames, transforms, re encodes or reformats that
        path, and no target that would do so may ever be added here. That makes the read-only
        guarantee structural rather than a matter of reviewer diligence.

      * One source of truth means the fixture cannot drift from the oracle. A second checked in
        copy could later be "corrected" by a maintainer, and the two documented mistranslations
        this resource carries must survive verbatim rather than being silently fixed.

      * The copy must stay byte identical to the original: 6824 bytes, no byte order mark, no XML
        declaration (the document opens directly with the pfw element), UTF-8 encoded Chinese, LF
        only line endings, and a final closing element with no trailing newline. The repository
        .gitattributes declares no eol and no text=auto rule, so no checkout normalization occurs
        and a plain copy preserves every byte. Never introduce an encoding conversion, a newline
        fixup or any other transform here; a size or hash mismatch in the output directory means
        the read-only guarantee has been broken.

    Content rather than None, and rather than EmbeddedResource, because the behaviour under test is
    reading a real file from a real relative path on disk, not streaming an assembly resource.
    PreserveNewest keeps incremental builds cheap while still refreshing the copy if the oracle is
    ever updated upstream.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Include="../../pfw.i18n.xml" Link="pfw.i18n.xml" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
